{"id": "EUVD-2026-55820", "enisaUuid": "ae9d5807-d315-353b-bd71-d1c0c3277a59", "description": "A flaw was found in odh-dashboard. An authenticated user of the dashboard can exploit a vulnerability related to how RoleBindings are created. The system does not properly validate the `roleRef` field, allowing a user to specify an arbitrary role, including highly privileged ones like `cluster-admin`. This can lead to privilege escalation, where an attacker gains unauthorized elevated access within their namespace and potentially persistent control over the system.", "datePublished": "2026-08-10T20:45:05", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-28T09:48:14", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:53261", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:53262", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:53263", "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-18950", "https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2511170"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-18950", "GHSA-jcjp-44w9-2wwj"], "assigner": "redhat", "epss": 0.52, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "00b126cb-8fd9-36ed-bc7d-fe0cc379b21b", "product": {"name": "Red Hat OpenShift AI 3.4", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1786109665"}, {"id": "4ff13ed7-745c-3c82-9eed-6722d381c733", "product": {"name": "Red Hat OpenShift AI 2.25", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1785940823"}, {"id": "e20f37cb-2c6e-30b3-98ec-de149bcc34b0", "product": {"name": "Red Hat OpenShift AI 3.3", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1786109683"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "1fb1f38f-9923-34b4-8979-1271c0ebcf35", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}], "isExploited": false}